("Which nerve must be anesthetized to numb the buccal gingiva of the mandibular molars?",
 "Long buccal nerve", ["Lingual nerve", "Mental nerve", "Nasopalatine nerve"],
 "The long (buccal) nerve, a branch of V3, supplies the buccal gingiva of the mandibular molars. The inferior alveolar block does not reliably reach it, so a separate buccal injection is given."),
("Which muscle of mastication is the only one that helps open the jaw?",
 "Lateral pterygoid", ["Medial pterygoid", "Temporalis, posterior fibers", "Masseter"],
 "The inferior head of the lateral pterygoid pulls the condyle forward and helps depress the mandible. The masseter, temporalis and medial pterygoid elevate it."),
("Lymph from the tip of the tongue and the lower lip midline drains first to which nodes?",
 "Submental nodes", ["Parotid nodes", "Occipital nodes", "Retropharyngeal nodes"],
 "The submental nodes drain the chin, the midline of the lower lip, the tongue tip and the mandibular incisors, then empty into the submandibular or deep cervical nodes."),
